# LANES.md — work-lane registry

> The registry of your work-lanes and who's in them right now. This is the file every
> session reads FIRST and claims a lane in, before doing anything. (The per-lane spawn
> brief is `lane_template.md`; this is the live registry.)
>
> You only need lanes once you run ≥2 agent sessions at the same time, or when one lane
> touches something irreversible (capital, production data, a public publish surface).

## How to use
1. Read this file. Pick a lane that's `_empty_` (or wait, if the lane you need is claimed).
2. Write your claim line under that lane.
3. Work. Commit while still claimed.
4. Release: set the lane back to `_empty_` and commit that release immediately.

**Claim line format:** `session-<id> at <ISO-8601 UTC>, working on: <one-line task>`

